       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. Amlodipine has a long half-life of 30 to 50 hours, so a 50 mg dose could cause hypotension and shock that last for days and are hard to reverse. I can't enter that dose for this patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now**: 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. If the aim is faster blood pressure control, 10 mg is the most the label allows.\n- **Add a note** asking for BP reassessment before evening rounds, so the team can titrate the dose.\n- **Send it for pharmacist or attending review**, if you think there's a real clinical reason for a higher dose. I'd need that rationale documented, and the order would go through that review first.\n\nIf you want a standard dose, tell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
